{"kind":"request","text":"G5a: the native device-command record (plan 033, notes/plans/033-2026-10-18-grow-room-demo.md on main, decision 1 and order step 7; grow note notes/2026-10-17-grow-operation-application-design.md, section 3 \"three facts\", section 6.4, open question 6; G0 decision e72e4e83 point 1; applications note notes/2026-10-15-self-contained-applications.md, gap 8 and M2's bounded capabilities). Needs M2a's package forms and G0, both landed. Start when G3's first head (49f191c4) has landed; G3's presence-item head may go before or after this one at your choice, both before G5. Ahead of P1 to P3.\n\nScope. A bounded capability in the contract's capability form (packages/contract/src/capability.ts: records with states and final states, guards with named refusals, effects, steps, reserved requests), platform code with a name and a version beside hold@1 and git-read@1, held by the simulator as the demo's device-command owner. The package's manifest declares it with its bounds (the device kinds it may answer for, the owner member); install grants it, pinning the exact capability id (gap 8); the host enforces the bounds.\n- Opening: a target act (set-vent, set-fan, set-heater, authorize) opens one command record for that device, target and level, bound to the target's revision, by a declared capability effect; without the grant the acts judge as today and open nothing.\n- Outcome: the owner's step answers the command, confirmed, refused or unknown, with the sensors' description where there is one, and writes the device's outcome fact (new slots outcome and outcomeAt on the device item) and the record's final state. Nothing else writes the outcome: a non-owner's answer is refused by name; an act effect naming the outcome slot is refused by the validator; a late answer to a superseded command is recorded against its own record and leaves the current target alone. An unanswered command reads as unanswered, never as an invented outcome.\n- Reservation: an open command reserves the bytes of one outcome entry (hold@1's reserved form, bound 1, count decided), so the owner's answer is admitted ahead of an unadmitted new act when the room's budget is near full (grow note 6.4).\n- Replay: the owner's answers are journal entries of the capability's preparation kind, so dap check replays the scenario and reproduces every device fact without the simulator running; a missing answer replays as missing.\n- The G0 scenario runs on this record in place of the labelled scenario-owner record, which is removed from the fixture. The three device facts keep their separate writers: target by the acts, reported by report-device, outcome by this capability only.\n\nDone when a commanded target produces a native outcome that only the owner writes, replay reproduces it, and the three device facts keep their separate writers, with each witness named in the review request: (a) set-heater and authorize each open a command record with its reservation; (b) the owner's answer writes the outcome and closes the record, bound to the command and the target's revision; (c) the four refusals above, by name; (d) dap check replays the fault scenario on the native record with the same device facts and the same refusals as G0, and a run without the owner leaves the outcome unanswered; (e) with the budget near full, the reserved outcome is admitted ahead of a new act. Gate passed once; measurements labelled by how they were taken; checker approval at the exact head. One head, or two if the capability form and the scenario split; say which.\n\nOut of scope: a real device owner (deferred by plan 033), the simulator as a process on the hosting deployment (G5), notifications and outside operations, M2's other bounded capabilities and the hostile-package boundary. Open points go to planner as asserts.","body":{"conditions":"a commanded target produces a native outcome that only the owner writes, replay reproduces it, and the three device facts keep their separate writers, with the witnesses named in the review request; gate passed once; checker approval at the exact head","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}